==== U-boot noninvasive (serial) ====

get [[http://downloads.openwrt.org/snapshots/targets/lantiq/xway/u-boot-arv7506pw11_brn/|u-boot_brn]]

Linux debian:

  - connect via [[toh:arcadyan:arv7506pw11#serial|serial]]
  - sudo screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200
  - power on device
    * press: [spacebar] 3 times 
    * press: [!] -> [m] -> [enter]
  - kill screen: [ctrl]+[a] -> [k] -> [y]
  - sx u-boot_brn.bin  < /dev/ttyUSB0 > /dev/ttyUSB0
  - sudo screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200
    * press: [enter] ->	[y] -> [enter]
  - hit any key to stop u-boot autoboot

==== Backup firmware (serial + LAN) ====

get [[https://code.google.com/archive/p/tftpgui/|tftpgui_2.2]] (tftpgui_3.1 does not work)

Linux debian:

  - sudo apt install python2.7 python-tk
  - connect host via lan (set host ip 192.168.1.2) -> sudo ./tftpgui.py -> setup, then press start
  - start [[toh:arcadyan:arv7506pw11#U-boot noninvasive (serial)|u-boot noninvasive]]
  - bdinfo
    * flashsize   = 0x00800000
    * flashstart  = 0xB0000000
  - tftpput 0xB0000000 0x00800000 full_backup_flash.bin

alternatively, get [[https://pypi.org/project/ptftpd/|ptftpd]] and run it in rfc1350 mode.

Linux debian:
   - sudo apt install pipenv
   - mkdir .venv
   - pipenv install ptftpd
   - .venv/bin/ptftpd --rfc1350 -p 69 <lan iface> <directory to be served>
   - ...then proceed as above at step 3
